  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing - diagnosis: **host directory permission / ownership** blocking writes.\n\nFactual claims with evidence:\n\n* Both containers are `running` - `incidentlab-app-1 Up 4 seconds`, `incidentlab-db-1 Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1).\n* App `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n* App runs as user `1000:1000` with bind `source /srv/lab-data -> destination /data rw:true` (E3).\n* App logs show initial `POST /upload 200 OK` then later `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` with `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/...part' -> '/data/uploads/...'` in `/app/main.py line 63 os.replace` (E4).\n* Health check in same logs fails for same reason: `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/uploads/.health...'` in `/app/main.py line 116` resulting in `GET /health 503` (E4).\n* Host path `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `owner_uid 0 owner_gid 0 mode 0755` with `app_uid 1000 app_gid 1000 app_user_can_write false` (E5).\n* Parent `/srv/lab-data` is `owner_uid 1000 owner_gid 1000 mode 0755 app_user_can_write true` (E6) - problem isolated to `uploads` sub-directory, not parent, not read-only mount.\n* Filesystem holding `/srv/lab-data` has `use_percent 9.0` `available_mb 410.6` `inode_use_percent 0.2` (E7) - rules out disk-full / inode-full.\n* Database container `running healthy restart_count 0 oom_killed false` (E8), logs `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors (E9) - rules out DB dependency as cause. App 503 is symptom of local write failure, not DB.\n* Recent Docker events show orderly `stop/die exit 0 / destroy / rename / start` recreates and `health_status: healthy` for db, no crash loop (E10).\n\nRoot cause vs symptoms:\nRoot cause is filesystem permission: container user 1000 cannot write to `/data/uploads` because host directory is owned by root with 0755.\nSymptoms are `500` on `/upload` and `503` on `/health`, both from `PermissionError` attempting to create files under that directory.\n",
